    "lawCode": "Amd §1612, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A8767A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to a qualified\ncapital investment at no more than one vendor track in Sullivan county\n\nPURPOSE: This bill will facilitate the investment of over six hundred\nmillion dollars for capital improvements at and adjacent to the Monti-\ncello Race Track.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS: Section 1 of the bill amends clause (G) of\nsubparagraph (ii) of paragraph 1 of subdivision b of section 1612 of the\ntax law as amended by section 1 of part 0-1 of chapter 57 of the laws of\n2009. The number of permanent employees to be hired is reduced from\n2,000 to no fewer than 1,000. The \"Qualified Capital Investment\" is\nreduced from one billion to six hundred million dollars. The\nconstruction of the Convention Center has been removed from the project\nleaving \"at least one eighteen hole golf course, and the construction\nand issuance of certificates of occupancy for hotels, lodging, spas,\ndining, retail and entertainment venues, parking garages and other capi-\ntal improvements at or adjacent to the licensed video gaming facility or\nlicensed vendor track.\"\n\nThe \"recapture amount\" has been increased:\n\n(i) One hundred percent (up from sixty-six percent) if the employment\nshortfall is greater than sixty-six and 2/3rds percent (up from fifty\npercent) of the employment goal.\n\n(ii) Seventy-five percent (up from sixty percent) if the employment\nshortfall is greater than thirty-three and 1/3rd percent (down from\nforty percent) of the employment goal.\n\n(iii) Forty-nine and 1/2 percent (up from forty-five percent) if the\nemployment shortfall is greater than thirty percent (no change) of the\nemployment goal.\n\n(iv) Twenty-two percent (up from twenty percent) if the employment\nshortfall is greater than twenty percent (no change) of the employment\ngoal.\n\n(v) Eleven percent (up from ten percent) if the employment shortfall is\ngreater than ten percent (no change) of the employment goal.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: Due to the economic crisis which severely impacted the\nbanking industry last fall and which continues to today, the ability of\nthe developer to secure financing for the project at the previous thres-\nhold was impacted. The developer has firm commitments for financing at\nsix hundred million dollars. Approval of this legislation will allow the\ndeveloper to begin construction on the project at this lower level of\nfinancing.\n\nSTATEMENT IN SUPPORT: This bill will facilitate the investment of over\n600 million dollars for capital improvements at and adjacent to the\nMonticello Race Track. In particular, this bill will support the devel-\nopment of a hotel and golf course at the former site of the Concord\nHotel. This bill therefore will help to revitalize the Catskill region\nby providing at least 1,000 full-time permanent jobs, as well as thou-\nsands of construction-related jobs during the construction period. More-\nover, this bill will guarantee a stream of funding to education that\nwill double the current VLT revenues at Monticello Race Track.\n\nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS: There is no State Fiscal Plan impact.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
